{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00779",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.06,
      "end_seconds": 15.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.65,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. It's my nose again. I thought the operation would sort it, but it's blocked again. Is it always going to be like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.55,
      "end_seconds": 23.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Let's have a proper look. When was the operation? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.6,
      "end_seconds": 36.75,
      "duration_seconds": 10.15,
      "text": "Eight months ago. The septum, and the turbinates. And it was lovely for about three months. Then it started creeping back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.78,
      "end_seconds": 42.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Which side is blocked?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.67,
      "end_seconds": 51.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "The left, mainly, and sometimes the right. Worse at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.7,
      "end_seconds": 59.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Anything else, discharge, loss of smell, pain in your face? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.06,
      "end_seconds": 66.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "Clear drip, sometimes. No pain. My smell's okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.9,
      "end_seconds": 73.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "What are you using for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.81,
      "end_seconds": 85.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "The steroid spray, fluticasone, two sprays each side once a day, though I confess I don't use it every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.96,
      "end_seconds": 94.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Thanks for being honest. What else is in your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.3,
      "end_seconds": 98.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Hay fever, and asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.71,
      "end_seconds": 102.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.66,
      "end_seconds": 108.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "I vape. Not smoke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.55,
      "end_seconds": 115.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Let me check you. Pulse and oxygen. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.78,
      "end_seconds": 119.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.49,
      "end_seconds": 135.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Pulse 72, oxygen 99 percent, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.81,
      "end_seconds": 140.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "All good? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.32,
      "end_seconds": 168.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.32,
      "text": "All good. Now I'll look up your nose with the light. Tilt your head back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.43,
      "end_seconds": 173.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Is it bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.66,
      "end_seconds": 189.71,
      "duration_seconds": 14.05,
      "text": "Your nasal lining is pink and swollen on both sides, particularly the left, and the septum looks straight, which is good. There's no pus and no polyps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.13,
      "end_seconds": 195.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "So what's wrong, then? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.3,
      "end_seconds": 218.16,
      "duration_seconds": 20.86,
      "text": "The swelling of the lining is what's blocking it, probably from your hay fever and the lining reacting, but I can't rule out some scarring inside from the surgery, which we can't see from here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.17,
      "end_seconds": 221.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Scarring? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.85,
      "end_seconds": 228.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Adhesions, occasionally. It's possible, though not likely. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.51,
      "end_seconds": 233.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "What do I do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.51,
      "end_seconds": 248.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.07,
      "text": "Use the fluticasone spray every day, even when you feel clear, for at least six weeks, because it only works when it's regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.1,
      "end_seconds": 253.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I'll set a reminder. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.71,
      "end_seconds": 264.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Add a salt-water rinse in the evenings, to clear the crusts and soothe the lining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.64,
      "end_seconds": 271.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Do I make it myself? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.63,
      "end_seconds": 278.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "You can buy sachets at the pharmacy. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.51,
      "end_seconds": 284.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Right. And if it doesn't help? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.97,
      "end_seconds": 299.9,
      "duration_seconds": 13.93,
      "text": "If you're still blocked after six weeks of regular use, come back and I'll refer you back to the ENT surgeon, who can look inside with a camera."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.69,
      "end_seconds": 306.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "I understand. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
